    "who": "owner",
    "message": "For offline sync of saved trails, should I use last-write-wins or something smarter?",
    "messageId": "b102942b-6703-4289-a4ba-6f54ff65b17b",
    "isAddedToHistory": true,
    "sentAt": 1785995940000
  },
  {
    "who": "leon",
    "message": "For saved trails, **last‑write‑wins per field** is enough: conflicts are rare (one person, a few devices) and the data is not collaborative. Keep an `updated_at` per field (or per small group of fields), and never LWW the track points themselves — those are immutable once recorded.\n\nCRDTs would be overkill unless you add shared trip planning later.",
    "messageId": "b102942b-6703-4289-a4ba-6f54ff65b17b:leon",
